Theme 1: Eval design is a creative discipline, not just a technical checkbox.
Recommendation: Invest in people who deeply understand your domain and what "good" looks like, rather than treating evaluation as a purely engineering task to be automated away.

Theme 2: The decision to rely on "vibes" versus rigorous evals is fundamentally a business ROI calculation.
Recommendation: Before defaulting to either approach, explicitly quantify the cost of building a proper eval pipeline against the actual revenue or retention impact of the quality improvements it would deliver.

Theme 3: Rigorous evaluation becomes non-negotiable when failures carry outsized consequences.
Recommendation: If your product operates at scale, touches high-stakes decisions, or competes primarily on output quality, treat a robust eval framework as critical infrastructure rather than a nice-to-have.

